      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The side advocating for teaching about systemic racism and power struggles is pushing for a more nuanced and accurate representation of history, acknowledging the complexities and injustices that have shaped the country. In contrast, the side focusing on the \"good things\" that made the country great is attempting to sanitize the past and avoid confronting the darker aspects of American history, which can be seen as a form of historical revisionism. By prioritizing the former, educators can foster critical thinking and empathy in students, rather than simply peddling a sanitized narrative.",
      "source": "target",
